Government content is not covered by that licence
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Ariane reads public Indian government websites and documents and records what
they say. The repository therefore contains, alongside its own source code:

  * URLs of government pages
  * titles of government pages and documents
  * short verbatim quotations from those pages, kept as the evidence behind
    every fact the product states
  * structured facts derived from them (services, documents, fees, timelines,
    offices, helplines, eligibility rules)

None of that material is ours, and the Apache-2.0 licence above does not and
cannot relicense it. The copyright in each government page and document remains
with the body that published it, and each is subject to the terms of the site
it came from. Quotations are retained for attribution and verification: a claim
you cannot trace back to its source is a claim this project does not want to
make. If you redistribute or build on this data, the terms of the original
sources are yours to check and to honour.

Nothing here is an official government publication, and nothing here is legal
advice. Government requirements change. Always confirm against the official
source, which every screen in Ariane links to for exactly that reason.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The evidence corpus is deliberately not in this repository
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Building the graph involves fetching and caching thousands of government page
bodies and PDFs. Those cached bodies are the third-party content described
above, in full, and republishing them is not something this project is entitled
to do. So the public repository ships the layer that is ours to publish, which
is the extracted facts, the quote behind each one, and the URL and retrieval
date it came from, and does not ship the page bodies themselves.

Everything a normal clone needs works without the corpus: `pnpm gates` and
`pnpm build` are green on a fresh checkout. The checks that reconcile citations
against saved page bodies live under `pnpm gates:corpus` and read a corpus you
point at with ARIANE_CORPUS_DIR. `fixtures/demo/` carries one small synthetic
page and the layers derived from it so the full chain is testable by anyone.

